.TH smi-build-package "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-build-package \- Build one or more downloaded SMI packages from source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-build-package
.I PACKAGE_NAME...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-build-package
runs the build function of the named packages, the step between
.BR smi-download-package (1)
and
.BR smi-install-package (1):
.PP
.RS
.nf
smi-download-package python313      fetch and unpack the sources
smi-build-package python313         configure and make, in the download directory
smi-install-package python313       make install, into /opt
.fi
.RE
.PP
It uses the
.B packages.sh
library to locate the package definitions, with the
.B .package
suffix, in the system or home packages directory, and calls the
.IB package _build_func
of each one.
The sources are read from the packages download directory, see
.BR smi-home-packages-location (1),
which defaults to
.B ~/.setmy.info/packages
and can be overridden with
.SM SMI_HOME_PACKAGES_DIR.
.PP
A package that has no build function is reported as
.RB \(dq "Nothing to build for package" \(dq
and is not an error: most packages ship a binary archive that only has to be unpacked, so
downloading and installing them is all there is.
.SH PACKAGES WITH A BUILD STEP
.PP
These are built from source and need this command:
.TP
.BR python39 ", " python310 ", " python311 ", " python312 ", " python313 ", " python314
.B ./configure
and
.B make
in the unpacked source directory.
.TP
.B erlang
.B ./configure
and
.B make
in the git checkout of the OTP tag, without wx, debugger, observer, et and javac.
.TP
.B elixir
.B make clean compile
in the git checkout of the version tag.
.TP
.B smi
.B ./configure release
and
.B make all test package
in the git clone, which produces the rpm that
.BR smi-install-package (1)
then installs.
.TP
.B all
Builds every package of its list that has a build function and skips the rest.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
One Python version, the three steps:
.RS
.nf
smi-download-package python314 && smi-build-package python314 && smi-install-package python314
.fi
.RE
.PP
Download on one machine, build and install on each:
.RS
.nf
smi-download-package erlang elixir
smi-build-package erlang elixir
smi-install-package erlang elixir
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every build function succeeded, or the packages had none.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
